Fixed: IBAMR::StaggeredStokesOperator, IBAMR::VCStaggeredStokesOperator, and IBAMR::CIBStaggeredStokesOperator now fill ghost values and apply boundary conditions only on the levels of their vectors, and the Stokes projection, VC projection, and block-factorization preconditioners fill ghost values only on those levels, so that a PETSc Krylov coarse solver of a Stokes FAC preconditioner no longer crashes. These classes and the preconditioners now stop with an error when the coarsest level of their vectors is above 0, because they need data on every coarser level.
<br>
